{
  "rule": "line-picker",
  "note": "How the footer picks a line. index: for a pool of `size` lines, the line shown for each hour counter in `seeds` — every round of `size` hours is a seeded shuffle (Mulberry32 seeded with cycle * 0x9E3779B1 + size * 0x85EBCA6B in 32-bit arithmetic, Fisher-Yates from the end), a round never starts with the line the last one ended on, a pool of one or none is always 0, and a pool of two alternates. keys: the pools a joke is drawn from, in order (night, hot from 28 C, cold to 2 C, monday/friday/weekend, then the kind, an unknown kind being cloud). dayOfWeek: 0 Sunday .. 6 Saturday of an ISO date, null if it isn't one. Kotlin: LinePicker; web: line-picker.ts.",
  "cases": [
    {"name": "a pool of none or one is always the first line",
      "fn": "index",
      "input": {
        "size": 1,
        "seeds": [
          0,
          1,
          99,
          -4
        ]
      },
      "expect": {
        "indexes": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          0
        ]
      }
    },
